Toolkit change for feat/settings-display-audio: screen choice and vsync for
the macOS Metal window, master volume and output device for the SDL audio
backend, and controller rumble from cellPadSetActDirect.

A diff against the ps3recomp-fork/ working tree as of 2026-10-17 (fork
770660a + ps3recomp-fork-770660a-with-upstream-prs.patch + that day's
uncommitted work). Touches libs/video/rsx_metal_backend.{m,h},
libs/audio/cellAudio.c, libs/input/cellPad.c and adds two unit tests
(libs/audio/tests/test_audio_settings.c, libs/input/tests/test_pad_rumble.c).
New variables: PS3_DISPLAY, PS3_VSYNC, PS3_AUDIO_VOLUME, PS3_AUDIO_DEVICE,
PS3_RUMBLE, PS3_RUMBLE_STRENGTH, PS3_RUMBLE_LOG. Unset, every one of them
leaves today's behaviour, except that rumble now reaches the controller at
the strength the title asks for (the small motor used to get 1/255 of full
and every request stopped after 100 ms).

Apply from the repo root, rebuild, then fold it into
ps3recomp-fork-770660a-with-upstream-prs.patch as usual and delete this file:
    git -C ps3recomp-fork apply --check ../infamous2-lle/patches/pending/settings-display-audio-rumble.patch
    git -C ps3recomp-fork apply ../infamous2-lle/patches/pending/settings-display-audio-rumble.patch

